  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to Water Sector Development in Africa 2005-2009</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Danish support to the African Development Bank&apos;s (AfDB) water and sanitation sector should be seen as a contribution to the continent&apos;s efforts to achieve the 2015 targets for sustainable development.

The funds are channeled through 3 water initiatives by the AfDB, and they hereby also represents the programmes components: 

1. The Rural Water Supply and Sanitation Initiative (RWSSI)
2. The African Water Facility (AWF) 
3. The Water Partnership Programme
 
The grant covers a total of DKK 300 million over a 5 year period (2005-2009). The grant is allocated as follows: AWF: 40, RWSSI: 230, WPP: 15. The remaining DKK 15 million will be administered by the MFA for technical assistance (3 million), monitoring &amp; reviews (5 million) and unallocated funds (7 million). 

The Danish support is provided in addition to assistance from other multilateral and bilateral partners.</narrative>
  </description>
